  "final_test_sha256": "97e001081af552751772650b5ba6791a07ec2735b7e092599908f1c528bd509b",
  "qualifications": [
    "Public dispatch uses in-process real PyOCDSWDInterface and real target_control, not production worker pipes or live hardware.",
    "Native Session constructor/configuration with probe is real. Session.open lifecycle and unavailable-AP/core discovery are boundary simulations. Real NRF52.is_locked/check_flash_security/mass_erase/persist_unlock and CoreSightTarget.check_for_cores run unmodified.",
    "Initial first-public exploratory configured routes used read-only production probe enumeration (UID 683854191); fake selected sessions failed construction before open. Subsequent tests isolate enumeration. No target session/hardware write/protection change or live grant occurred.",
    "Initial first/second-public failures and two pyright failures are retained; no production failure was established by those fixture/type mistakes.",
    "Earlier sensitivity identity output identified contextlib for the decorated fixture; final identities use inspect.unwrap and identify actual tiered_acceptance_support.py.",
    "Initial snapshot reconstruction diagnostics failed (Windows path key, then two hash mismatches); command logs and exact input SHA256 identities remain retained. Pre-change exact initial test body was not archived; later snapshots are stored by hash.",
    "Base adapter format drift remains FAIL as separately disclosed by ROOT; no adapter format check was rerun or relabeled.",
    "Silent nRF54 decline, physical transport behavior, current-board protection and Nordic erase remain unproved. No protected-target recovery feature or module acceptance is claimed."
  ]
}
